import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 622 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 623 | 2026-10-22 | **Keys and staff rebuilt from scratch in the final Scales look.** Her complaint (2026-10-22): the small-house and big-house colours were too alike, the same sentence repeated in the title and the line, and the lessons felt fitted into the old ones. The whole concept is new (`kq.jsx`, shared `KqEngine`): keyboards are `ScKeys` with the note letters above the keys, small house (2 black keys, C D E) in coral and big house (3 black keys, F G A B) in blue, the chosen key solid (new `MARK_STYLE.pickB`), the staff only behind a 'Show on the staff' button. Each screen says three different things: the title names the idea, the line adds one new fact, the right/wrong feedback says something else. 23 lessons in five sections: (1) Keyboard patterns and note names (kq-groups, kq-hear, kq-small, kq-big, kq-find, kq-middle, kq-repeat); (2) The staff and clefs (kq-lines, kq-treble, kq-bass, kq-grand, kq-climb); (3) Line and space names (kq-ntreble, kq-nbass, kq-landmarks, kq-count, kq-read); (4) Ledger lines and 8va (kq-above, kq-below, kq-middlec, kq-8va); (5) Pitch and range (kq-size, kq-range). The old Keys and staff block (KsBox, KpRoofs, KsEngine, KS_SPEC and the rest) is gone. Built by `patch633.py` (+ `kq.jsx`) (`t637`). Opened every lesson at 390 px in English and Korean (all, one by one, her turn, right and wrong answers) and the Home concept page with open sections kept when coming back from a lesson: no console errors. **For her review (facts not from her material):** Queen's G on line 2, King's F on line 4, treble C in space 3, bass C in space 2, middle C on a ledger line, 8va = one octave higher, long bars sound low, piano A0-C8, 12 keys = 7 white + 5 black; Korean wording is Claude's. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
